// 010.15 (D37, #56, #45): `Share` and `ProRata` with explicit `Remainder To` conserving every cent,
// 2-argument `Min`/`Max`, and `Applies amt To v1, v2, ...` payment waterfalls.
Fact spouse Identified by Elena, Sam
Fact member Identified by Alice, Bob, Carol
Param pool = $15,000.01
Param dividend = $100.00
Function shares Identified by member * int
Fact spouse-award Identified by spouse * USD
Fact member-payout Identified by member * USD

Event split-marital
  Creates (Foreach spouse: spouse-award(spouse, Share(pool Among spouse Remainder To Elena)))

Event pay-dividend
  Creates (Foreach member: member-payout(member, ProRata(dividend By shares Among member Remainder To Alice)))

Role debtor Is Dana
Role creditor Is Ines
Var fees : USD = $50.00
Var interest : USD = $120.00
Var principal : USD = $1,000.00
Act remit Actor debtor Recipient creditor Related to payment : USD
  Holds when payment > $0
  Applies payment To fees, interest, principal
.
split-marital().
?spouse-award(Elena, $7,500.01).
?spouse-award(Sam, $7,500.00).

+shares(Alice, 1). +shares(Bob, 1). +shares(Carol, 1).
pay-dividend().
?member-payout(Alice, $33.34).
?member-payout(Bob, $33.33).
?member-payout(Carol, $33.33).

?(Min($80.00, $50.00) == $50.00).
?(Max($80.00, $50.00) == $80.00).

// Remitting $200 clears $50 fees, $120 interest, and $30 of principal -> $970 remaining:
remit($200.00).
?(fees == $0.00).
?(interest == $0.00).
?(principal == $970.00).
